  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 313 AM CDT Thu May 21 2026\n\nThis morning's RAP analysis indicated a surface high pressure was \ncentered over Lake Superior/Upper MI, bringing mostly clear skies \nand calm/light winds to much of northern WI. These conditions aided \nin surface temps dropping into the low 30s along the WI/Upper MI \nborder, but mid-level clouds were keeping temperatures across \ncentral and east-central WI in the low to mid 40s. Therefore, the \ncurrent Frost Advisory in effect for the Northwoods until 8 AM \nremains on track. Considered upgrading counties along the WI/Upper \nMI border to a Freeze Warning, but the amount of time below freezing \nis expected to be too brief or too localized.\n\nRain Chances...Due to the proximity of the surface high pressure, \ndry conditions with periods of mid-level clouds are expected to \ncontinue today through at least Friday afternoon. Model guidance is \nstill indicating two systems will approach the region for the start \nof the Memorial Day weekend, one from the south and one from the \nwest. The latest guidance would suggest only a portion of eastern WI \nmay get clipped by the northwest precip shield of the southern \nstream system late Friday night into Saturday, while portions of \ncentral and north-central WI could see light precip from the other \nsystem on Saturday and perhaps Sunday, but forcing appears weak. \nAdditional weak shortwaves look to bring chances for showers and \nstorms at times through the middle of next week as well.\n\nTemperatures...Another cooler day is expected for today with high\ntemperatures about 10-15 degrees below normal ranging from the \nmid 50s to low 60s. Lows tonight are expected to be chilly again \nranging from the mid 30s across the Northwoods to low 40s south. \nThe potential for frost development across the Northwoods tonight \nis low at this time due to anticipated cloud cover. Temperatures \nwill gradually warm each day through the Memorial Day weekend, \nrising above normal by Sunday with highs in the 70s. Upper- level \nridging and southerly flow looks to bring temps into the 80s for \nMemorial Day through at least midweek.",
